---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Nav from "../components/Nav.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";

const title = "Privacy Policy — AnySpace";
const description =
  "How AnySpace collects, uses, and protects your information. Local-first by default; this policy covers the cloud-touching exceptions.";
const lastUpdated = "May 11, 2026";
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <Nav />
  <main id="main" class="py-16 sm:py-20">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
        <aside
          class="mb-10 rounded-lg border border-border bg-bg-elev px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-fg-muted"
          role="note"
          aria-label="Draft notice"
        >
          <strong class="text-fg">Draft — pending legal review.</strong>
          This document is a placeholder so the footer links resolve. It has not
          been reviewed by counsel and is not yet in force. Final language will
          replace it before any paid signup or production cloud feature ships.
        </aside>

        <p class="mb-2 font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-fg-dim">
          Last updated: {lastUpdated}
        </p>

        <article class="docs-prose">
          <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
          <p>
            AnySpace is a desktop workspace for terminals, editors, previews,
            and AI agents. This Privacy Policy explains what information we
            collect, how we use it, who we share it with, and the rights you
            have over it. AnySpace is <strong>local-first by design</strong>:
            most of what you do in the app stays on your machine and never
            reaches us. The sections below focus on the pieces that <em>do</em>
            cross the network.
          </p>

          <p>
            For a technical, file-by-file inventory of what AnySpace sends over
            the network and what it stores locally, see{" "}
            <a href="/docs/reference/privacy">Privacy &amp; data handling</a>{" "}
            in the docs. That page is the practical companion to this legal
            statement.
          </p>

          <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
          <p>
            AnySpace is operated by <strong>Rebase LLC</strong> ("AnySpace",
            "we", "us"). For privacy questions, contact{" "}
            <a href="mailto:support@anyspace.dev">support@anyspace.dev</a>.
          </p>
          <p>
            Registered address: <em>[address pending]</em>. State of formation:{" "}
            <em>[state pending]</em>.
          </p>

          <h2>2. Scope</h2>
          <p>This policy covers:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>The AnySpace marketing website (this site).</li>
            <li>The AnySpace desktop application.</li>
            <li>
              <strong>AnySpace Cloud</strong>, our optional managed endpoint for
              AI and speech-to-text requests.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            It does <strong>not</strong> cover third-party AI, speech-to-text,
            or other providers that you configure in the app yourself
            (OpenAI, Anthropic, Groq, ElevenLabs, etc.). When you point
            AnySpace at one of those providers, your data goes directly to that
            provider under their terms, not ours.
          </p>

          <h2>3. What we collect</h2>

          <h3>Account information (when you sign in)</h3>
          <p>
            Authentication is handled by <strong>Clerk</strong>. When you sign
            in, Clerk processes your email address, password (hashed), and any
            OAuth provider claims you grant (e.g., Google profile, GitHub
            username). A minimal copy of your user record is mirrored to our
            backend so we can associate it with subscriptions and Cloud usage.
          </p>

          <h3>Billing information (when you purchase a plan)</h3>
          <p>
            If and when paid plans are available, billing is handled by a
            third-party payment processor. We receive the metadata necessary to
            manage your subscription (plan, status, last four digits of the
            card, billing email). We do <strong>not</strong> store full card
            numbers.
          </p>

          <h3>AnySpace Cloud usage (when you opt in)</h3>
          <p>
            If you route AI or speech-to-text requests through AnySpace Cloud,
            those requests transit our infrastructure. We log request metadata
            (timestamp, model, token counts, latency, error codes) for billing,
            abuse prevention, and operational debugging. Request and response
            payloads are not retained beyond the time required to serve the
            request, unless we are legally required to preserve them.
          </p>

          <h3>Site analytics</h3>
          <p>
            This website may collect aggregate, non-identifying usage data
            (page views, referrers, country-level location) to understand how
            the site is used. We do not run advertising trackers.
          </p>

          <h3>What we do not collect</h3>
          <p>
            AnySpace does not transmit any of the following to us, ever:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>Your local settings, kanban tasks, or agent definitions.</li>
            <li>
              Your terminal scrollback, command history, or shell session data.
            </li>
            <li>Files in your project folders.</li>
            <li>Screenshots from the screenshot stack or Live Preview.</li>
            <li>
              Team-mode coordination files in{" "}
              <code>&lt;projectFolder&gt;/.anyspace/teams/</code>.
            </li>
            <li>
              Super Agent conversation history (stored only in the local
              SQLite DB on your machine).
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            See <a href="/docs/reference/privacy">the technical docs</a> for a
            full file-by-file breakdown.
          </p>

          <h2>4. How we use information</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>To provide, operate, and improve AnySpace and AnySpace Cloud.</li>
            <li>To authenticate you and secure your account.</li>
            <li>To process payments and manage subscriptions.</li>
            <li>
              To prevent abuse, fraud, or violations of our{" "}
              <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>.
            </li>
            <li>To communicate with you about your account or the service.</li>
            <li>To comply with legal obligations.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2>5. Third-party processors</h2>
          <p>We rely on the following processors to operate AnySpace:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>Clerk</strong> — authentication and identity management.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Cloudflare</strong> — content delivery and edge hosting
              for this website and AnySpace Cloud.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Payment processor</strong> — billing for paid plans
              (named here once a processor is selected).
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Separately, AI and speech-to-text providers that <em>you</em>{" "}
            configure in the app — including OpenAI, Anthropic, Groq,
            ElevenLabs, and any other endpoint you point AnySpace at — are
            <strong> not our subprocessors</strong>. Your data reaches those
            providers because you sent it there. Their handling of that data
            is governed by their own policies.
          </p>

          <h2>6. Sharing and disclosure</h2>
          <p>We do not sell your personal information. We share it only:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              With the processors listed above, strictly to provide the
              service.
            </li>
            <li>
              When required by law, court order, or a valid government request.
            </li>
            <li>
              To protect the rights, property, or safety of AnySpace, our
              users, or the public.
            </li>
            <li>
              In connection with a merger, acquisition, or sale of assets, in
              which case we will notify affected users.
            </li>
          </ul>

          <h2>7. Data retention</h2>
          <p>
            We retain account and billing information for as long as your
            account is active and for a reasonable period afterward to comply
            with legal, accounting, and audit obligations. AnySpace Cloud
            request logs are retained for a limited operational window (target:
            30 days) and then deleted. Anything that stays on your machine
            stays on your machine until you delete it.
          </p>

          <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
          <p>
            Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access,
            correct, delete, or export your personal information, to object to
            or restrict certain processing, and to withdraw consent. These
            include rights under the EU/UK GDPR and the California Consumer
            Privacy Act (CCPA/CPRA).
          </p>
          <p>
            To exercise any of these rights, email{" "}
            <a href="mailto:support@anyspace.dev">support@anyspace.dev</a>. We
            will respond within the time periods required by applicable law.
          </p>

          <h2>9. International transfers</h2>
          <p>
            AnySpace is operated from the United States. If you access the
            service from outside the United States, your information will be
            transferred to, stored, and processed in the United States or
            another country where we or our processors operate. We rely on
            appropriate safeguards (such as standard contractual clauses) where
            required.
          </p>

          <h2>10. Children</h2>
          <p>
            AnySpace is not directed to individuals under 16. We do not
            knowingly collect personal information from children under 16. If
            you believe a child has provided us with personal information,
            contact us and we will delete it.
          </p>

          <h2>11. Security</h2>
          <p>
            We use industry-standard administrative, technical, and physical
            safeguards to protect personal information. No method of
            transmission or storage is 100% secure, however, and we cannot
            guarantee absolute security.
          </p>

          <h2>12. Changes to this policy</h2>
          <p>
            We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. When we do,
            we will revise the "Last updated" date at the top. Material changes
            will be communicated through the app or by email.
          </p>

          <h2>13. Contact</h2>
          <p>
            Questions or requests:{" "}
            <a href="mailto:support@anyspace.dev">support@anyspace.dev</a>.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>
